course: dictionary
lesson: 1568
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word character has several meanings, so you must use the context to find the right one. Ask: who or what is this sentence about? Then choose the meaning that fits.
explain: «The way a character speaks, posh, rough, local or old-fashioned, helps to show what they are like.» Here a character is a person in a story, because the sentence is about how people talk in a book or film.
explain: «Christians believe the Holy Spirit grows good character in people, like fruit on a tree.» Here character means the kind of person you are inside: honest, kind or brave. Swap in the meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
explain: «Chinese writing uses thousands of characters.» Here a character is a letter, number or symbol used in writing, not a person at all. Always test your meaning in the sentence before you decide.
fact: A character can be a person or animal in a story, film or play.
fact: Your character is the kind of person you are inside, such as brave, kind or honest.
fact: A character can also be a letter, number or symbol used in writing.
fact: «Out of character» means not like the way someone usually behaves.
fact: Context clues help you choose the right meaning of a word with more than one meaning.
exercise: «In many good stories a character changes by the end.» In this sentence, what does character mean? | A kind, honest person | *A person or animal in a story | A password | A letter, number or symbol
exercise: «Her kindness and honesty show her strong character.» What does character mean here? | A symbol used in writing | *The kind of person she is inside | A funny, unusual person | A person in a film
exercise: A computer asks for a password with at least eight characters. What does character mean? | A person in a story | A brave and honest person | An unusual person | *A letter, number or symbol
test: «Dad says Mia is a real character.» What does a real character mean here? | A letter used in writing | A person who is always honest | *An interesting, unusual person | A person in a play
test: «He shouted at his sister, which was out of character for him.» What does out of character mean? | Written in a password | Exactly like him | *Not like the way he usually behaves | Written in a book
exam: «The main character of the book lost her way in the forest.» What does character mean here, and how do you know? | A password, because it has more than one letter | A symbol in writing, because books have letters | The kind of person she is inside, because she is lost | *A person in a story, because the sentence is about a girl who gets lost in a book
